                                                "sense_id": "a27dd81f-c9c5-336c-8a2b-f33dfeb1794b",
                                                "text": "In place of a stinger, a male bee or wasp has hardened genitalia […] used for grasping the female during mating and transferring sperm. Male genitalia are a showcase of structural plasticity."
